  "id": "collapsing",
  "term": "collapsing",
  "definition": "In this psychology context, collapsing refers to boundaries or distinctions becoming less separate, such as between self and other or between past and present. It describes a merging in psychological meaning that makes something feel more personally relevant or immediate.",
